        <body>
            <div xml:id="d526">

                <pb facs="0864" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg728"/>

                <head>No. 526.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 6, 1888</date>.
                        (Received June 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 766.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instructions numbered 875
                    of May 17, and to previous correspondence, I have the honor to inclose herewith,
                    for your information, certain extracts from the Times of June 1, containing the
                        <pb facs="0865" n="729" xml:id="pg729"/> report of speeches made in the
                    House of Commons on the 31st ultimo, by Mr. McArthur, Sir James Fergusson, and
                    Mr. Bryce, with respect to Germany’s action in Samoa.</p>
                <p>I have, etc</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d526-a1.xml" xpointer="d526-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
